s\n\nStatus\n    open\n\nImportance\n    Research corpus\n\nSolutions\n    0\n\nLess than 1 year old · traced to 2026\n\nLet a lattice path from $(0,0)$(0,0) to $(n,n)$(n,n) be a word in $\\{E,N\\}^{2n}${E,N}2 n, and say that two paths are even-intersecting if they have an even number of common edges. Let $C_n$C n​ denote the $n$n th Catalan number.\n\nCatalan classification conjecture. There are exactly $C_n$C n​ families of size $2^n$2 n in which every two distinct paths have an even number of common edges.\n\nThe even-intersection theorem shows that $2^n$2 n is the maximum possible size, while the paper constructs at least $C_n$C n​ distinct extremal families, one for each noncrossing perfect matching of $[2n]$[2 n]. The conjecture asserts that these constructions exhaust all extremal families.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nUmesh Shankar, “Oddtown and eventown theorems for lattice paths”, arXiv:2607.23117 (2026).\n\nextremal-combinatoricslattice-pathsset-systems\n\nPosted 1 month ago\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSum Rule for the Eight-Vertex Model on Its Combinatorial Line (https://ouci.dntb.gov.ua/en/works/7B1RxXD9/)\nciteturn8search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Cantini, L.: qKZ equation and ground state of the O(1) loop model with open boundary conditions (2009). arXiv:0903.5050 ... Di Francesco, P., Zinn-Justin, P.: Around the Razumov–Stroganov conjecture: proof of a multi-parameter sum rule.\nDOI: 10.1088/1751-8113/43/8/085206\n  7. Cantini, L.: qKZ equation and ground state of the O(1) loop model with open boundary conditions (2009). arXiv:0903.5050\n  8. Cantini, L.: Finite size emp